WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.543 --> 00:00:05.919
I’m Ukrainian.

00:00:06.545 --> 00:00:09.422
And my country is fighting
a war for survival.

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:14.261
But there is another war
where we all must fight.

00:00:14.261 --> 00:00:16.012
Fight for the future of the planet.

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:19.474
It's a war against climate change.

00:00:20.892 --> 00:00:25.605
Both of them have dramatic consequences
for the future of our lives.

00:00:26.147 --> 00:00:28.149
Both are killing thousands.

00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:31.444
And the root cause of both

00:00:31.486 --> 00:00:33.613
is overdependence on fossil fuels.

00:00:34.406 --> 00:00:38.326
Today, I want to explain
how Ukraine's energy challenge

00:00:38.326 --> 00:00:41.413
can help the world
to fight climate change.

00:00:42.539 --> 00:00:43.790
For decades,

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:49.004
Russia has been weaponizing energy
to impose control over countries.

00:00:49.462 --> 00:00:52.132
It has cut gas supply during the winter,

00:00:52.716 --> 00:00:56.136
bribed us with cheap gas,

00:00:56.177 --> 00:00:59.598
built pipelines to bypass Ukraine

00:00:59.598 --> 00:01:03.351
and under-supply gas
to provoke energy shock

00:01:03.393 --> 00:01:05.729
that hurt all of us.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:07.689
But today,

00:01:07.689 --> 00:01:09.482
Russia moved from economic war

00:01:09.524 --> 00:01:12.694
to physical destruction
of our infrastructure,

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:18.491
launching missiles to destroy
our power stations and grids

00:01:18.491 --> 00:01:20.994
and trying to crush the Ukrainian people.

00:01:21.953 --> 00:01:24.414
I get to see the impact every day

00:01:24.456 --> 00:01:25.957
running DTEK,

00:01:25.999 --> 00:01:29.169
one of the largest Ukrainian
power suppliers.

00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:31.129
When I wake up every morning,

00:01:31.129 --> 00:01:35.342
my first job is to see
whether we've been hit and how bad.

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:37.469
Since the beginning of this war,

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:40.805
our company was attacked
more than 10,000 times.

00:01:41.181 --> 00:01:46.102
A hundred of DTEK employees
have been killed on a military front line

00:01:46.102 --> 00:01:48.647
or serving on energy front line behind.

00:01:49.356 --> 00:01:54.152
These attacks expose not only
Ukraine's vulnerability, but the world's.

00:01:54.653 --> 00:01:59.407
Almost every economy on earth
depends on massive,

00:01:59.449 --> 00:02:04.162
highly centralized but easily
targeted energy systems

00:02:04.204 --> 00:02:07.582
used to extract and burn fossil fuels.

00:02:08.083 --> 00:02:12.212
But now in Ukraine,
the war is teaching something new.

00:02:12.921 --> 00:02:15.715
That relying on renewable power,

00:02:15.757 --> 00:02:20.136
we create much more resilient
and secure energy system.

00:02:20.553 --> 00:02:24.057
To understand why, 
picture a wind turbine.

00:02:24.099 --> 00:02:25.266
It's big.

00:02:25.266 --> 00:02:29.020
700 tons and 130 metres tall.

00:02:29.437 --> 00:02:32.691
But actually, the footprint
is just a few meters.

00:02:33.024 --> 00:02:36.361
It's hard to be attacked by missiles

00:02:36.403 --> 00:02:40.573
and if they succeed one, all other
wind turbines are still running.

00:02:41.408 --> 00:02:43.702
This kind of distributed power systems

00:02:43.743 --> 00:02:47.580
combined with the energy
from household solar panels,

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:51.710
can massively enhance energy security
of countries all over the world.

00:02:52.627 --> 00:02:55.213
And not only during war time,

00:02:55.255 --> 00:02:58.466
but against other threats
like fires and floods.

00:02:59.259 --> 00:03:03.930
Ukraine is becoming a testing ground
for a new energy future.

00:03:04.347 --> 00:03:06.975
After the first invasion in 2014,

00:03:07.016 --> 00:03:11.438
Russia destroyed or captured more
than 30 percent of DTEK power assets.

00:03:12.313 --> 00:03:16.109
Our response was to double
renewable capacity,

00:03:16.151 --> 00:03:19.070
helping Ukraine to become the country

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:22.741
with one of the highest growth rates
of renewables in the world.

00:03:23.867 --> 00:03:28.163
One real life example
and symbol of our resilience

00:03:28.204 --> 00:03:31.458
is the Tiligulska wind farm
on the coast of the Black Sea,

00:03:31.499 --> 00:03:33.793
just 60 miles from the front line.

00:03:34.836 --> 00:03:37.797
Through the first 15 months of the war,

00:03:37.839 --> 00:03:42.093
we built wind farm
without foreign contractors,

00:03:42.135 --> 00:03:45.805
sometimes with missiles
flying above our heads

00:03:45.847 --> 00:03:48.641
and spending a lot of time
in bomb shelters.

00:03:48.683 --> 00:03:50.018
And we succeeded.

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:56.065
From May 2023, we supply green energy
produced by this wind farm

00:03:56.065 --> 00:03:59.402
to more than 200,000 households.

00:03:59.444 --> 00:04:02.489
And we are planning
to expand this wind farm

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:05.825
to become one of the largest
in Eastern Europe.

00:04:06.576 --> 00:04:09.037
War in Ukraine forced Europe

00:04:09.037 --> 00:04:13.249
to end its dependence
on dirty Russian energy

00:04:13.291 --> 00:04:15.794
through accelerating green transition.

00:04:16.753 --> 00:04:19.297
And Ukraine can play a key role

00:04:19.339 --> 00:04:23.134
by becoming a major supplier
of clean energy to Europe.

00:04:23.551 --> 00:04:27.180
With the right level
of foreign investments,

00:04:27.222 --> 00:04:30.767
Ukraine can build enough
renewable capacity by 2030

00:04:30.767 --> 00:04:32.560
to supply Europe

00:04:32.602 --> 00:04:36.981
as much clean energy as countries
like Finland produce during the year.

00:04:37.899 --> 00:04:43.696
The vision of Ukraine -- greener,
and facing west towards Europe --

00:04:43.738 --> 00:04:49.035
is even embraced by thousands
of DTEK coal miners

00:04:49.035 --> 00:04:51.913
serving on the front line against Russia.

00:04:53.164 --> 00:04:57.126
So when do we launch
this green counteroffensive?

00:04:57.460 --> 00:05:01.714
The smart move is not to wait,
but to accelerate

00:05:01.756 --> 00:05:05.802
so that we meet
the climate crisis challenge

00:05:05.844 --> 00:05:08.596
to establish energy independence

00:05:08.596 --> 00:05:11.641
and to build much more
resilient energy systems.

00:05:11.683 --> 00:05:15.979
A green transition will help
to win both of these wars

00:05:15.979 --> 00:05:18.022
and secure a lasting peace.

00:05:18.064 --> 00:05:20.024
(In Ukrainian: Glory to Ukraine).

